      "iast": "nimittaṃ manaścakṣurādipravṛttau\nnirastākhilopādhirākāśakalpaḥ |\nravirlokaceṣṭānimittaṃ yathā yaḥ\nsa nityopalabdhisvarūpo’hamātmā ||1||"
    },
    {
      "id": "hastamalaka-stotram-2",
      "label": "Verse 2",
      "number": "2",
      "deva": "यमग्न्युष्णवन्नित्यबोधस्वरूपं\nमनश्चक्षुरादीन्यबोधात्मकानि ।\nप्रवर्तन्त आश्रित्य निष्कम्पमेकं\nस नित्योपलब्धिस्वरूपोऽहमात्मा ॥२॥",
      "translation": "Like the heat of fire, I am the one unmoving Self whose nature is eternal awareness; mind, eye, and the other faculties, insentient by nature, function by depending on that one.",
