      "iast": "yamagnyuṣṇavannityabodhasvarūpaṃ\nmanaścakṣurādīnyabodhātmakāni |\npravartanta āśritya niṣkampamekaṃ\nsa nityopalabdhisvarūpo’hamātmā ||2||"
    },
    {
      "id": "hastamalaka-stotram-3",
      "label": "Verse 3",
      "number": "3",
      "deva": "मुखाभासको दर्पणे दृश्यमानो\nमुखत्वात् पृथक्त्वेन नैवास्ति वस्तु ।\nचिदाभासको धीषु जीवोऽपि तद्वत्\nस नित्योपलब्धिस्वरूपोऽहमात्मा ॥३॥",
      "translation": "A reflection of a face seen in a mirror is no real thing separate from the face. Likewise, the individual self appearing in intellects as a reflection of consciousness is not separate from consciousness. I am that Self, whose nature is ever-present awareness.",
