    },
    {
      "id": "hastamalaka-stotram-4",
      "label": "Verse 4",
      "number": "4",
      "deva": "यथा दर्पणाभाव आभासहानौ\nमुखं विद्यते कल्पनाहीनमेकम् ।\nतथा धीवियोगे निराभासको यः\nस नित्योपलब्धिस्वरूपोऽहमात्मा ॥४॥",
      "translation": "Just as, when the mirror is absent and the reflection has vanished, the one face remains free of imagined multiplicity, so when the intellect is absent, the one without a reflected appearance remains. I am that Self, whose nature is ever-present awareness.",
